---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import Illustration from '../components/Illustration.astro';
import NextSteps from '../components/NextSteps.astro';
import Ticker from '../components/Ticker.astro';

const approachTags = ['Psychodynamic', 'Attachment-Based', 'Relational', 'Depth-Oriented', 'Collaborative'];

const frameworks = [
  {
    name: 'Psychodynamic',
    copy: 'We explore what lives beneath the surface: the patterns, defenses, and relational dynamics that operate outside awareness and shape your inner life.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Attachment-Based',
    copy: 'Your earliest relationships left a blueprint. We look at how that blueprint shows up in how you connect, trust, and protect yourself today.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Collaborative',
    copy: 'Therapy itself is a relationship. What unfolds between us becomes a live window into the patterns we are working to understand and change together.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Depth-Oriented',
    copy: 'Symptoms often carry meaning. Together, we make space to understand what they are expressing, so change can take root at a deeper level.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Psychodynamic Therapy Approach | Newport Beach & Fullerton"
  description="Psychodynamic, attachment-based therapy in Newport Beach & Fullerton, CA. Understand the 'why' behind your patterns — for lasting change, not quick fixes."
  active="/approach/"
  path="/approach/"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow">Effective, depth-oriented psychotherapy</p>
      <h1>Explore your past. <br>Own your present. <br><em>Build your future.</em></h1>
      <p>
        We all carry stories that shape how we think, feel, and connect. Deep change happens
        when we honor the full range of our lived experiences and make sense of the narratives
        shaping our lives.
      </p>
      <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Schedule a free consultation <span class="arw">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <img src="/approach.svg" alt="Abstract illustration of nested ellipses and circles forming a sphere, representing depth-oriented psychotherapy" class="hero-figure approach-hero-art" width="248" height="341" />
  </section>

  <Ticker items={approachTags} label="Approach" variant="blue" />

  <!-- Philosophy -->
  <section class="section split c-narrow-wide">
    <div class="col gap-20">
      <p class="eyebrow">MY APPROACH</p>
      <h2 class="h2-serif">Connecting deeper,<br><em>living freer.</em></h2>
      <Illustration name="expansion-full" size="260px" color="var(--blue)" class="hero-figure mt-16" />
    </div>
    <div class="prose prose-15">
      <p>We are shaped by the relationships, experiences, and stories that surround us. Some of these stories bring connection and belonging while others leave imprints of pain, shame, or self-doubt. Over time, we develop ways of being with ourselves and others that reflect those early experiences. Some of these patterns serve us well; others leave us feeling stuck, disconnected, or unsure of how to move forward. So much of this happens outside our immediate awareness, shaping our relationship to ourselves and others in ways we can’t quite grasp. This is where therapy can help.</p>
      <p>Many of the people I work with come to therapy looking for answers to the deep questions about why they’re struggling, or with a sense that their best attempts to change on their own aren’t working. Using a psychodynamic, depth-oriented approach, we explore the “why” behind your feelings and behaviors — tracing how your foundational experiences became the template for the way you connect today.</p>
      <p>As those patterns come into view, they begin to loosen their hold. You can move through your relationships and choices more freely, consciously, and more connected to yourself and the people around you. This can lead you to inhabit your life in a way that feels truer to who you are, what you value, and what’s meaningful to you.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quote -->
  <section class="quote-block">
    <img src="/quote.svg" alt="" class="hero-figure" width="270" height="229" />
    <div class="col gap-28">
      <blockquote>“The past influences everything and <em>dictates nothing.</em>”</blockquote>
      <cite>Adam Phillips</cite>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How I work -->
  <section class="section sage on-color">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow on-color">HOW I WORK</p>
        <h2 class="h2-serif">What shapes how I work with you.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Our work together creates space for making sense of what feels painful or repetitive: persistent challenges with anxiety, depression, intimacy and closeness, loss, patterns of self-sabotage, emotional expression, or a desire to feel more at ease with yourself.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ruled-grid cols-2 frameworks" style="margin-bottom:56px">
      {frameworks.map((f) => (
        <div class="ruled-cell">
          <div class="label framework-name">{f.name}</div>
          <p style="color:inherit">{f.copy}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="card-row">
      <a class="service-card primary" href="/services/individual-therapy/"><span>Individual therapy</span><span class="arw" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a class="service-card secondary" href="/services/couples-therapy/"><span>Couples therapy</span><span class="arw" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:28px; font-size:15px">
      Specialty care: <a class="inline-link" href="/services/premarital-counseling/">premarital counseling</a>, <a class="inline-link" href="/services/therapy-for-anxiety/">therapy for anxiety</a>, and <a class="inline-link" href="/services/therapy-for-creatives/">therapy for creatives</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- What to expect -->
  <section class="section split c-media">
    <Portrait src="/office-photo.jpeg" alt="Nikole's therapy office" placeholder="Office or session photo" />
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow">What to expect</p>
      <h2 class="h2-serif">Our work <em>together.</em></h2>
      <p class="body">Healing unfolds in its own time. Our work together will honor that rhythm, building trust and welcoming all parts of your experience. Because no two people arrive with the same story, I tailor our work to you. I believe meaningful healing is made possible through a relationship grounded in safety, trust, and genuine care.</p>
      <p class="body">We’ll meet regularly, making room for both what is easy to put into words and what remains less clear. Together, we’ll notice the threads between your emotions, relationships, past experiences, and the ways you have learned to move through the world. Over time, this can open new perspectives and possibilities that feel more aligned with who you are and what you value.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/about/">About Nikole <span class="arw">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextSteps
    heading="Getting <em>started.</em>"
    copy="If what you’ve read sounds interesting to you, reach out. I offer a free 15-minute consultation to give you a chance to ask questions and get a feel for how we might work together."
  />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Portrait-orientation hero art — size by width and center in the column. */
  img.approach-hero-art {
    width: clamp(260px, 32vw, 380px);
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: block;
  }
  /* Framework cells stack the title above the copy (rather than the shared
     row layout) and color the title with the lime accent. */
  .frameworks .ruled-cell {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .framework-name {
    color: var(--lime);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
